  "description": "Test 14, derived by hand from 10. Record: u16 version 2, ref adjusted grid, ref raw grid (object IDs 2 and 3 after the simulator's 1, foundations 2.7 [choice]; class 0x49B9E602), f32 globalMultiplier, u8 average, u32 count, count x (s32 x, s32 z, s32 weight). For (0.95, 50, [(11,10,3)]) the bytes after the references are 33 33 73 3F 32 01 00 00 00 0B 00 00 00 0A 00 00 00 03 00 00 00 (39 bytes in all). Write -> read -> write is byte-identical and the grids come back with their values. Versions 1 and 3 are rejected (Read returns false before reading anything; the store ignores the result, foundations 3.5, so the check is the state left: multiplier 0, average 0, no grids). A truncated hotspot list stops the read (fields read so far are kept; [choice] the count starts at 0 and the loop stops at the first failed read), as does a count of 0xFFFFFFFF with no data. Init on a loaded city keeps the loaded grids (no grid created), keeps the saved multiplier (14.2), and the first SimNewDay runs the empty EndOfCycle that clears the hotspots and the average (14.1). [choice] (14.4) a loaded grid whose tract size is not 1 is shut down at Init and replaced by a new grid. Read appends (10 [compat]): reading record 'a' into a used simulator holding hotspots [(1,2,5)], candidates [(4,4,1)] and zoned sum 9 gives [(1,2,5), (11,10,3)], multiplier 0.95 and average 50, and keeps the candidates and the zoned sum. A record whose adjusted-grid reference names an unknown class (0x12345678) puts the stream in error there: both grid slots are left null (foundations 2.7: a reference read nulls its destination first, and the raw reference fails on the errored stream), the multiplier and the average keep their values and no hotspot is appended (count 0, the spec's [choice]).",
